<body>
    <h1>Troubleshooting: Pixstore commands not in path of client system</h1=
>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"Troubleshooting:Pixstorecommandsnotinpathofclientsystem-G=
PFSCommands:RunasrootOnly(PATHSetup)">GPFS Commands: Run as <strong>root</s=
trong> Only (PATH Setup)</h1>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:Pixstorecommandsnotinpathofclientsystem-Why">Why<=
/h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>GPFS tools fan out over SSH and manage cluster state.</p></li>
<li>
<p>For safety and consistency, we run them <strong>as root only</strong> (n=
o permission changes on <code>/usr/lpp/mmfs</code>).</p></li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:Pixstorecommandsnotinpathofclientsystem-OptionA=
=E2=80=94Usearootshell(sudo-i)andsetPATHforroot">Option A =E2=80=94 Use a r=
oot shell (<code>sudo -i</code>) and set PATH for root</h2>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Open a root login shell:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo -i
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p>Add GPFS bin to <strong>root=E2=80=99s</strong> PATH (persistent):</p></=
li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">cat &gt=
;&gt; /root/.bashrc &lt;&lt;'EOF'
# GPFS (Spectrum Scale) tools in PATH for root
if [ -d /usr/lpp/mmfs/bin ] &amp;&amp; [[ ":$PATH:" !=3D *":/usr/lpp/mmfs/b=
in:"* ]]; then
  export PATH=3D"$PATH:/usr/lpp/mmfs/bin"
fi
EOF

cat &gt;&gt; /root/.profile &lt;&lt;'EOF'
# Ensure PATH for login shells
if [ -d /usr/lpp/mmfs/bin ] &amp;&amp; [[ ":$PATH:" !=3D *":/usr/lpp/mmfs/b=
in:"* ]]; then
  export PATH=3D"$PATH:/usr/lpp/mmfs/bin"
fi
EOF
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p>Reload and verify:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">source =
/root/.bashrc
which mmgetstate
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<blockquote>
<p>From now on, in a root shell, just run:</p>
</blockquote>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">mmgetst=
ate -a
mmstartup
mmmount mmfs1 -N per-ai
mmlsmount mmfs1
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:Pixstorecommandsnotinpathofclientsystem-OptionB=
=E2=80=94Keepusingsudo<cmd>fromyouruser">Option B =E2=80=94 Keep using <cod=
e>sudo &lt;cmd&gt;</code> from your user</h2>
<p>By default, <code>sudo</code> uses its own <strong>secure_path</strong> =
which might not include GPFS. Add it <strong>for sudo only</strong> (does n=
ot affect non-root users).</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Edit sudoers safely:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo vi=
sudo
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ol start=3D"2">
<li>
<p>Append (or merge with existing <code>secure_path</code>) so it includes =
<code>/usr/lpp/mmfs/bin</code>:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Default=
s secure_path=3D"/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/b=
in:/usr/lpp/mmfs/bin"
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ol start=3D"3">
<li>
<p>Verify:</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo wh=
ich mmgetstate
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<blockquote>
<p>Now you can run:</p>
</blockquote>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo mm=
getstate -a
sudo mmmount mmfs1 -N per-ai
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:Pixstorecommandsnotinpathofclientsystem-OptionC=
=E2=80=94Lightweightroot-onlyshims(noPATHedits)">Option C =E2=80=94 Lightwe=
ight root-only shims (no PATH edits)</h2>
<p>Create tiny wrappers in <code>/usr/local/sbin</code> (already in root=E2=
=80=99s PATH). These call the real binaries but still require root to be us=
eful.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo te=
e /usr/local/sbin/mmgetstate &gt;/dev/null &lt;&lt;'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
exec /usr/lpp/mmfs/bin/mmgetstate "$@"
EOF
sudo chmod 755 /usr/local/sbin/mmgetstate

for c in mmstartup mmmount mmlsmount mmumount mmshutdown; do
  sudo tee /usr/local/sbin/$c &gt;/dev/null &lt;&lt;EOF
#!/usr/bin/env bash
exec /usr/lpp/mmfs/bin/$c "\$@"
EOF
  sudo chmod 755 /usr/local/sbin/$c
done
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Verify:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo -i
which mmgetstate
mmgetstate -a
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"Troubleshooting:Pixstorecommandsnotinpathofclientsystem-Recommend=
edUsage">Recommended Usage</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Day-to-day:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">sudo -i=
           # become root
mmgetstate -a
mmmount mmfs1 -N per-ai
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>If you prefer staying as your user:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Use <strong>Option B</strong> once =E2=86=92 <code>sudo mmgetstate -a</c=
ode> works everywhere.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> We intentionally <strong>did not</strong> relax d=
irectory permissions on <code>/usr/lpp/mmfs</code> or expose GPFS to non-ro=
ot users.</p>
</blockquote>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
